  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seed potato multiplication in Angola</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The agricultural production in Angola dropped due to the civil war.The quantity and quality of the local food production is very low and cannot keep up with the growing demand. Therefore, seed- and consumer potatoes are imported, as well as most of the food of the country. Food shortages and high prices are common. The development of the potato sector is restrained due to a lack of quality seed potatoes necessary for the development of local production of consumer potatoes.The partners want to set up a joint venture and grow seed potatoes with a large workforce of full time employees and seasonal workers. The project introduces new cultivation techniques, pest control, pivot irrigation and a cold storage necessary for the dormancy period of the products. The seed potatoes will be sold to small and large farmers at a reasonable price. The project is situated in Huila province a 1,000 km south of Luanda. This higher region has a perfect climate for potato cultivation.The project has a positive impact on smallscale farmers who cannot afford the expensive import seed potatoes. The project is important in knowledge transfer on cultivation and storage techniques to the farmers and the whole sector. On a national level the project sets an example and contributes to food security.</narrative>
  </description>
